Z||000002||Homicidal||05-19-2000||05:58 PM||||hmmm.......4th generation firebird seats?  I dunno, best thing is to look at them.  To change your seats all you gotta do it remove the four retainer screws and take the seat out.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula||05-19-2000||06:46 PM||||ok, I too have a formula!!!!! and I too am 18!!!!!! and I too had the seat problem!!!!<P>take the seat out, look at it for a moment........<P>then find on the part that you pull up to tilt there will be a spring in there, reatach the spring and your done..... just like me!!!!<P>btw......WE NEED PICS||||reg||1
Z||000004||Coconut||05-19-2000||06:47 PM||||Hey Formula 18, Welcome aboard! You'll find that this is a very active forum with extremely helpful people. I'm sure you'll feel right at home. Enjoy your Formula! They are really nice rides. Post the pics when you can. About your seats, I'd go with Homicidal's suggestion, take them out of the car and allow yourself soom room to really inspect the mechanism and see whats up. Once you've determined what the problem is,you'll find the solution much easier.||||reg||14
Z||000005||Cooter||05-19-2000||10:40 PM||||I have a set of 4th gen Camaro seats in one of my 88GT's, complete with the seat tilt mechanism from the camaro. The drivers seat needs one of the mounting ears ground down a little (I believe it was the outer rear one). On the passenger seat, you must use the seat tracks from the Fiero on the new seats. It is a simple matter of swapping 4 bolts.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Flash Box||05-19-2000||11:29 PM||||Welcome aboard. I too am a new Fiero owner and the guys on this board have been great in answering my questions.||||reg||14
